# Testing Rules

## Framework

- Use Vitest for testing.
- Use Supertest for backend API integration tests.
- Use React Testing Library for frontend component and UI tests.
- Test through the Express application rather than individual controllers.

## General

- Write tests when implementing each feature.
- Every new endpoint must include integration tests.
- Frontend components and utilities should include automated tests where behavior is non-trivial.
- Cover both successful and failure scenarios.
- Do not mock business logic in integration tests.
- Keep tests independent and repeatable.

## Unit Tests

- Unit test pure utility modules.
- Status transition validation should have exhaustive unit tests.

## Backend Integration Tests

- Test complete request → response behavior.
- Verify HTTP status codes and response bodies.
- Verify database persistence where applicable.

## Frontend Tests

- Use React Testing Library to test rendered UI and user-visible behavior.
- Prefer queries by role, label, or accessible name over implementation details.
- Mock API modules when testing components that fetch data.
- Keep frontend tests focused on presentation, routing, and error display — business rules remain backend-tested.

## Test Environment

- Use a separate test database for backend integration tests.
- Seed required data before backend tests.
- Clean up data between backend tests.
- Frontend tests run in jsdom via Vitest; no database required.

## Quality

- Do not disable failing tests.
- Maintain existing test coverage.
- Run regression tests before completing a feature.